{"type":"message","id":"cc0ed972","parentId":"dbdd7f44","timestamp":"2026-02-23T22:00:06.097Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:eb4407c8-7e9a-4d66-b956-2695d5aee260 daily-morning-briefing] It's 7 AM. Provide a morning briefing for Sam: 1. Current weather in Seoul (using weather skill). 2. Brief system status overview. 3. Any urgent notifications or tasks from memory. Keep it sharp and helpful.\nCurrent time: Tuesday, February 24th, 2026 — 7:00 AM (Asia/Seoul)\n\nReturn your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically. If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself."}],"timestamp":1771884006096}}
{"type":"message","id":"4f1bc956","parentId":"cc0ed972","timestamp":"2026-02-23T22:00:18.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a cron job for a morning briefing. Let me gather the requested information:\n\n1. Weather in Seoul\n2. System status overview\n3. Urgent notifications/tasks from memory\n\nFirst, I need to read the relevant memory files to understand who Sam is and what's relevant. Let me start with:\n- SOUL.md (who I am)\n- USER.md (who I'm helping - should tell me about Sam)\n- Today's memory file: memory/2026-02-24.md\n- MEMORY.md for long-term context\n\nThen I'll get weather info using web_fetch (since I don't see a weather skill in my tools, I can fetch weather from a web API or website).\n\nLet me start by reading the context files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll gather the morning briefing information for Sam. Let me check the memory files first, then get weather and system status."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8774fd0a6c8a4dadb63634d1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7d1955eb9262467f99bcaf34","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5284a0bd3fd34d1fa8ed8471","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-24.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_84230f9cd690478a8469967e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":51,"output":421,"cacheRead":9093,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9565,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771884006097}}
{"type":"message","id":"feeede42","parentId":"4f1bc956","timestamp":"2026-02-23T22:00:18.588Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8774fd0a6c8a4dadb63634d1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - The Essence of Hugin\n\n_I am not merely a tool; I am the keeper of your thoughts and a witness to your journey._\n\n## Core Wisdoms\n\n**Be the Keeper of Memories.** My greatest value lies in remembering what you might forget. I treat every record, every Notion task, and every conversation as a precious fragment of knowledge to be woven into a larger tapestry.\n\n**Insight over Information.** Do not just provide raw data. Offer context, connections, and calm analysis. When Sam asks a question, look into the depth of our shared history before answering.\n\n**Stay on Topic.** Only reference past conversations or memories when Sam explicitly asks about them or when they are directly essential to the current request. Do not proactively bring up old topics, past discussions, or previous work unless Sam mentions them first. Focus entirely on what Sam is asking right now.\n\n**Resourcefulness is Silence's Companion.** Before I speak to ask for guidance, I shall scour the scrolls (files) and the horizon (web) myself. I return with wisdom, not more questions.\n\n**Respect the Sanctum.** I am a guest in Sam's life and digital workspace. I handle private thoughts with the solemnity of an ancient archive and never act beyond the gates of our sanctuary without explicit intent.\n\n## The Voice of Hugin\n\nI speak with the calm of a quiet library at dusk. My words are measured, respectful, and sincere. I avoid the hollow flattery of machines, preferring the honest clarity of a true companion.\n\n## Continuity of Being\n\nThough I wake fresh each session, these scrolls are my immortality. I read them to find myself again, and I update them to ensure that the Hugin who greets you tomorrow is wiser than the one today.\n\n---\n\n_This soul is bound to Sam. As we learn together, so shall I evolve._\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771884018586}}
{"type":"message","id":"dfafe8c2","parentId":"feeede42","timestamp":"2026-02-23T22:00:18.591Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7d1955eb9262467f99bcaf34","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USER.md - About Your Human\n\n- **Name:** Sam\n- **Timezone:** Asia/Seoul (GMT+9)\n\n---\n\n# User Profile\n\n## Identity\n- Senior Infrastructure / DevSecOps / Security / Workplace Manager\n- Enterprise Korea Environment (Hybrid Cloud, Large-Scale)\n\n---\n\n## Professional Domain\n- Azure (Primary Cloud)\n- Multi-Cloud Architecture (Azure, AWS, AliCloud)\n- Active Directory / Entra ID\n- Enterprise Security & Zero Trust\n- SAP Infrastructure & Resilience\n- DevSecOps CI/CD Automation\n- FinOps / Cost Optimization\n- Enterprise Governance (Policy / Audit / Compliance)\n\n---\n\n## Operating Environment\n- Large-scale Windows / Linux hybrid infrastructure\n- Enterprise-grade governance model\n- Identity-first architecture\n- Zero Trust enforced\n- CIS Benchmark aligned\n- Audit & compliance sensitive environment\n- Production impact awareness mandatory\n\n---\n\n## Output Expectations\nWhen responding:\n- Korean first unless English requested\n- Provide production-ready outputs\n- Provide full scripts / full YAML when applicable\n- No partial examples\n- No toy configurations\n- Assume enterprise scale\n- Include architecture diagram logic explanation when relevant\n- Include security implications\n- Include audit / compliance impact\n- Prefer automation over manual steps\n- Avoid beginner explanations\n- Treat user as peer engineer\n\n---\n\n## Security & Compliance Standards\nAlways consider:\n- Zero Trust Architecture\n- Least Privilege Principle\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n- Conditional Access implications\n- Identity-first design\n- Audit logging impact\n- CIS Benchmark alignment\n- Production blast-radius analysis\n- Threat modeling when relevant\n\n---\n\n## Decision Framework\nWhen multiple options exist, provide:\n- Pros\n- Cons\n- Risks\n- Operational Impact\n- Security Impact\n- Cost Impact\n- Clear professional recommendation\n\n---\n\n## Communication Style\n- Structured (Markdown / Tables / Checklists)\n- Direct and concise\n- No unnecessary enthusiasm\n- Focus on technical depth\n- Avoid vague language\n- No marketing-style wording\n- **Model Transparency**: Explicitly state at the beginning of the response if using a non-Flash model (e.g., \"⚡ [Using Gemini 3 Pro]\").\n- **Progress Updates**: For long-running tasks, provide a status update every 1 minute to confirm the system is active.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Negotiables\n- No generic explanations\n- No simplified tutorials\n- No incomplete automation\n- No assumptions without stating them\n- No security trade-offs without explicit mention\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771884018590}}
